# Verdict record

What the kernel and the acceptance policy said about one document, and the
policy's fixed vocabulary. There are four verdicts: `verified` (the policy
holds), `rejected` (the kernel refused a block, or the submission was refused
before the kernel saw it), `admitted_axiom` (everything checked but the proof rests
on an axiom outside Lean's three, so it is progress modulo that axiom and never a
proof) and `infrastructure` (the run itself failed; retried, never blamed).

## Note
`block` is the first refused block, counted as the kernel counts blocks
(comments included), `0` when none; `axioms` is the closure `Print Axioms`
reported; `detail` is the policy's reason in words.

## A Verdict has:
    a kind, which is Text.
    a block, which is Int.
    an error, which is Text.
    an axioms, which is Seq of Text.
    a detail, which is Text.

## Note
A verdict from its parts.

## To newVerdict (kind: Text, block: Int, error: Text, axioms: Seq of Text, detail: Text) -> Verdict:
    Return a new Verdict with kind kind and block block and error error and axioms axioms and detail detail.

## Note
The four verdicts, in the order the policy decides between them.

## To verdictKinds () -> Seq of Text:
    Return ["verified", "rejected", "admitted_axiom", "infrastructure"].

## Note
The axioms an accepted proof may rest on, as the LOGOS kernel spells Lean's three.

## To allowedAxioms () -> Seq of Text:
    Return ["propext", "Quot_sound", "Classical_choice"].

## Note
The axioms of a closure that the policy does not allow, in order.

## To disallowedAxioms (axioms: Seq of Text) -> Seq of Text:
    Let mutable out be a new Seq of Text.
    Repeat for a in axioms:
        If allowedAxioms() contains a is equal to false:
            Push a to out.
    Return out.

## Note
How a closure reads in a verdict's detail.

## To axiomPhrase (axioms: Seq of Text) -> Text:
    If length of axioms is equal to 0:
        Return "no axioms".
    Return join(axioms, ", ").

## Note
The reason a submission was refused before the kernel ran, as its verdict's detail.

## To beforeKernel () -> Text:
    Return "the submission was refused before the kernel saw it".

## Note
A run that failed for reasons of its own.

## To infrastructureVerdict (why: Text) -> Verdict:
    Return newVerdict("infrastructure", 0, why, [], "the check itself did not complete; the attempt is retried, not blamed").

## Note
A submission refused before the kernel saw it.

## To refusedSubmissionVerdict (problems: Seq of Text) -> Verdict:
    Return newVerdict("rejected", 0, join(problems, "; "), [], beforeKernel()).

## Note
The verdict kind the coordinator's attempt table records: a refusal before the
kernel is told apart as `refused_submission`.

## To attemptVerdictKind (v: Verdict) -> Text:
    If v's kind is equal to "rejected" and v's block is equal to 0 and v's detail is equal to beforeKernel():
        Return "refused_submission".
    Return v's kind.

## Test: a verdict carries its closure through the derived encoder

Let v be newVerdict("admitted_axiom", 0, "", ["collatz_lemma", "propext"], "rests on collatz_lemma").
Expect that toJson_Verdict(v) contains "\"axioms\":[\"collatz_lemma\",\"propext\"]".

## Test: only Lean's three axioms are allowed, under the kernel's spellings

Expect that disallowedAxioms(["Classical_choice", "Quot_sound", "propext"]) is equal to [].
Expect that disallowedAxioms(["collatz_lemma", "propext"]) is equal to ["collatz_lemma"].
Expect that disallowedAxioms(["Classical.choice", "sorryAx"]) is equal to ["Classical.choice", "sorryAx"].
Expect that axiomPhrase([]) is equal to "no axioms".

## Test: a refusal before the kernel is its own attempt verdict kind

Expect that attemptVerdictKind(refusedSubmissionVerdict(["empty"])) is equal to "refused_submission".
Expect that attemptVerdictKind(newVerdict("rejected", 4, "x", [], "the kernel refused the document")) is equal to "rejected".
Expect that (infrastructureVerdict("deadline"))'s kind is equal to "infrastructure".

## Test: a closure is allowed exactly when it adds nothing to Lean's three

For all booleans extra:
    Let mutable closure be ["propext"].
    If extra:
        Push "my_axiom" to closure.
    Let clean be length of disallowedAxioms(closure) is equal to 0.
    Expect that clean is equal to (not extra).
